  "body": "Moving this check to compile time in 1a249c2 restored the arrangement from\nbefore 905b721 ([WebDriver BiDi] enable and disable scripting via BiDi) and\nundid it: with scripting disabled through WebDriver BiDi an event handler IDL\nattribute returned null again, and an event handler whose value is a function\nran.\n\n\"Scripting is disabled\" bundles three conditions that want different treatment,\nso check them where they belong instead:\n\n* A null browsing context and the sandboxed scripts browsing context flag stop\n  an internal raw uncompiled handler from being compiled. This is what\n  implementations do, and it is all they do: an event handler IDL attribute set\n  to a function still runs in a document without a browsing context, and in\n  Chromium and Gecko in one sandboxed without allow-scripts.\n* WebDriver BiDi scripting being disabled stops the event handler from running,\n  while leaving the IDL attribute returning the function.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62719 and\nhttps://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/56715\n\n***\n\n/cc @sadym-chromium @zcorpan — sorry, #12944 was mine and I did not notice it\nwas undoing the event handler part of #11441.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (@sadym-chromium)\n   * WebKit\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62719 (landed)\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/56715 (landed)\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed: N/A\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: N/A\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13009/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 2, 2026, 2:58 PM UTC (a21db0c)\">/webappapis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13009/92f2480...a21db0c/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Oct 2, 2026, 2:58 PM UTC (a21db0c)\">diff</a> )",
